# ouroboros#172: a C-variable buffer REBIND releases the previous value (the
# old form leaked the whole old buffer on every rebind: 200k rebinds of a
# 256-buffer, AOT 421 MB peak RSS vs the VM's 2.9 MB; measured in the
# commit). Parity here: rebinds through buffer(), zeros(), a compiled
# function returning a buffer, an alias, and a rebind to itself.
b is buffer of 4
b[0] is 7
define fresh(n) as:
    local r is zeros of n
    r[0] is n
    return r
i is 0
loop while i < 3:
    b is buffer of 4
    b[1] is i
    i is i + 1
print of b
b is fresh of 5
print of b
c is b
b is zeros of 2
print of c
print of b
b is b
print of b
